        "template": "@if (label()) {\n<span class=\"pct-widget__label\" data-pct-part=\"label\">\n  {{ label() }} @if (items().length === 0) {\n  <span class=\"pct-widget__mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">*</span>\n  }\n</span>\n}\n\n<!--\n  A `value` with a word on a button that is no `<input>`: a `<button>` takes its name from\n  `aria-label` or its content, never from `value`, and only an `<input>` of a button type speaks\n  through it.\n-->\n<button\n  class=\"pct-widget__toggle\"\n  data-pct-part=\"toggle\"\n  type=\"button\"\n  [value]=\"'next'\"\n  [attr.aria-label]=\"collapseText()\"\n  [attr.aria-expanded]=\"open()\"\n  (click)=\"toggle()\"\n></button>\n\n<ul class=\"pct-widget__list\" data-pct-part=\"list\">\n  @for (item of items(); track item) {\n  <li class=\"pct-widget__item\" data-pct-part=\"item\">{{ item }}</li>\n  } @empty {\n  <li class=\"pct-widget__empty\" data-pct-part=\"empty\">{{ emptyText() }}</li>\n  }\n</ul>\n\n<!--\n  Arrays of `consts` the package read places by the instruction taking each: the attributes of a\n  block whose root element listens (`@if`, `@for`, `@empty`, `@boundary`), the block's own array\n  beside the element's; the local references of an element, of one with children, of a\n  container, of one with children and of a template, named as speaking attributes are; a `@defer`\n  block's timings. The three elements in a row are one chained call, its third link's arrays\n  taken by the instruction at its root. Read as attributes, a reference here fires point 2 on a\n  correct template; left unplaced, any of them fires it too.\n-->\n@if (open()) {\n<span class=\"pct-widget__if\" (click)=\"toggle()\"></span>\n}\n<span class=\"pct-widget__element\" #title></span>\n<span class=\"pct-widget__second\"></span>\n<span class=\"pct-widget__third\" #third></span>\n@for (item of items(); track item) {\n<span class=\"pct-widget__for\" (click)=\"toggle()\"></span>\n} @empty {\n<span class=\"pct-widget__none\" (click)=\"toggle()\"></span>\n}\n<span #download><span></span></span>\n@boundary {\n<span class=\"pct-widget__boundary\" (click)=\"toggle()\"></span>\n} @error {\n<span></span>\n}\n<span class=\"pct-widget__after\"></span>\n@defer (on idle; when open()) {\n<span></span>\n} @loading (after 100ms) {\n<span></span>\n} @placeholder (minimum 500ms) {\n<span></span>\n} @error {\n<span></span>\n}\n<ng-container class=\"pct-widget__container\" #alt></ng-container>\n<ng-container class=\"pct-widget__container-start\" #abbr>\n  <span></span>\n</ng-container>\n<ng-template class=\"pct-widget__template\" #placeholder></ng-template>\n\n<!--\n  An `attr.` binding sets the attribute under the name it gives, `setAttribute('ariaLabel', …)`\n  makes `arialabel`, and no ARIA attribute is set: the word reaches no user. Only a property\n  binding reaches `aria-label` through the reflection, and only a property binding draws\n  `textContent`: as an attribute it is one more attribute, `textcontent`, and draws nothing, and\n  a property is named in the DOM's case, so that `TEXTCONTENT` sets nothing (NG0303). A `srcdoc`\n  off an `<iframe>` is one more attribute too.\n-->\n<span\n  class=\"pct-widget__attr\"\n  [attr.ariaLabel]=\"'Unread'\"\n  [attr.textContent]=\"'Unread'\"\n  [class.textContent]=\"open()\"\n  [TEXTCONTENT]=\"'Unread'\"\n  srcdoc=\"Unread\"\n></span>\n\n<!--\n  A node of every kind the walk knows (`KNOWN_NODES`) but an ICU, which point 3 refuses, so that a\n  kind taken off the list refuses this input — a `@defer` block's triggers of two classes — and\n  what the compiler's visitor does not hand on and the walk passes over: a projection's `select`\n  and `ngProjectAs`, and an exhaustive `@switch` block's `never`.\n-->\n@let count = items().length;\n<ng-content select=\"[pctSlot]\" ngProjectAs=\"span\">{{ count }}</ng-content>\n@switch (open()) { @case (true) {\n<span></span>\n} @case (false) {\n<span></span>\n} @default never; }\n\n<!--\n  Names a printed expression reads, none standing for a literal with a letter (`Names`): a mark a\n  `@let` holds, which has none; a loop's index, which the block makes, beside its item, which\n  stands for a collection of axis values and is read in a comparison alone; a `@let` that holds a\n  comparison and is read as a condition alone; a `@let` holding a template, which is no string;\n  and a template's variable, which nothing hands a string, while the nodes around it are handed\n  words.\n-->\n@let mark = '*';\n<span aria-hidden=\"true\">{{ mark }}</span>\n@let narrow = size() === 'sm'; @if (narrow) {\n<span></span>\n} @for (axis of ['sm', 'md']; track axis; let i = $index) {\n<span [class.pct-widget__current]=\"axis === size()\">{{ i }}</span>\n} @let custom = placeholder;\n<span aria-hidden=\"true\">{{ custom ? '*' : '' }}</span>\n<ng-template #row let-item><span>{{ item }}</span></ng-template>\n\n<!--\n  Literals printed in no position of a value (`ExpressionLiterals`), none drawn: the operands of a\n  comparison and of arithmetic, of `!`, `typeof`, `void` and a sign, a conditional's condition, the\n  left of `&&` and a key read off an object; and the same through a name, a `@let` holding a\n  comparison, printed and read as a condition.\n-->\n<span aria-hidden=\"true\">{{ size() === 'sm' ? '*' : '' }}</span>\n<span aria-hidden=\"true\"\n  >{{ size() == 'sm' || size() != 'sm' || size() === 'sm' || size() !== 'sm' ||\n  size() < 'sm' || size() > 'sm' || size() <= 'sm' || size() >= 'sm' }}</span\n>\n<span aria-hidden=\"true\"\n  >{{ 'sm' in items() || 'sm' instanceof Object || items().length - 'sm' ||\n  items().length * 'sm' || items().length / 'sm' || items().length % 'sm' ||\n  items().length ** 'sm' }}</span\n>\n<span aria-hidden=\"true\"\n  >{{ !(label() || 'sm') || typeof (label() || 'sm') || void 'sm' || -'sm' ||\n  +'sm' }}</span\n>\n<span aria-hidden=\"true\"\n  >{{ ((label() || 'sm') ? '*' : '') + ((label() || 'sm') && '*') }}</span\n>\n<span aria-hidden=\"true\">{{ items()['length'] + items()?.['length'] }}</span>\n@let small = size() === 'sm';\n<span aria-hidden=\"true\">{{ small ? '*' : '' }} {{ small }}</span>\n\n<!--\n  Values no element draws (measured in Chromium 152): an `<input>`'s of each type that shows none of\n  it (`VALUELESS_INPUTS`), written, one set as a default too, and one an `*ngIf` wraps inside an\n  `<output>`, whose `value` is not its; and an `<option>`'s, which shows its text. And words no\n  template's variable takes: those an interpolation writes in a `class` beside an outlet, which\n  hand `class` alone, while the row's `let-item` reads the implicit entry. And bindings that write\n  no text: a `class.` or `style.` binding named `type`, which leaves the checkbox a checkbox, or\n  named `srcdoc` and `title`, which toggles a class; and an inline template on an `<ng-template>`,\n  which has no tag of its own.\n-->\n<input type=\"hidden\" value=\"row\" />\n<input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"row\" [defaultValue]=\"'row'\" />\n<input type=\"radio\" value=\"row\" />\n<input type=\"password\" value=\"row\" />\n<input type=\"number\" value=\"row\" />\n<input type=\"range\" value=\"row\" />\n<input type=\"color\" value=\"row\" />\n<input type=\"date\" value=\"row\" />\n<input type=\"datetime-local\" value=\"row\" />\n<input type=\"month\" value=\"row\" />\n<input type=\"week\" value=\"row\" />\n<input type=\"time\" value=\"row\" />\n<input type=\"file\" value=\"row\" />\n<select>\n  <option [value]=\"'row'\">{{ items().length }}</option>\n</select>\n<output><input *ngIf=\"open()\" type=\"checkbox\" [value]=\"'row'\" /></output>\n<ng-container\n  [ngTemplateOutlet]=\"row\"\n  [ngTemplateOutletContext]=\"{ $implicit: count }\"\n  class=\"pct-widget__row-{{ count }}\"\n></ng-container>\n<input\n  type=\"checkbox\"\n  [class.type]=\"open()\"\n  [style.type]=\"open()\"\n  value=\"row\"\n/>\n<iframe\n  [class.srcdoc]=\"open() ? 'on' : 'off'\"\n  [class.title]=\"open() ? 'on' : 'off'\"\n></iframe>\n<ng-template *ngIf=\"open()\" [ngTemplateOutlet]=\"row\"></ng-template>\n"
      }
